# Raw downloaded filings can be large — keep them out of git, they reproduce via `make fetch`
# (ABS-EE XML is fetched by a PINNED accession number -- an immutable EDGAR filing, so
# re-fetching always returns identical bytes; excluding it from git is safe.)
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep

# EXCEPTION: the Fed H.15 Treasury snapshot is NOT reproducible the same way -- it's a
# live daily series ("latest observations"), so a fresh fetch on a different day
# returns a different rate and can silently shift loan tiers across a risk threshold.
# Committing this snapshot pins the benchmark exactly like the deal accessions are
# pinned, so `make all` reproduces the SAME analysis, not just "a" analysis.
!data/raw/h15_treasury.csv

# Processed artifacts are regenerated by the pipeline
data/processed/*.db
data/processed/*.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Rendered output (optional final PDF)
analysis/findings.pdf

# Claude Code local session state (keep launch.json, which is shared config)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
